course: dictionary
lesson: 10085
title: Therapy: help to get better
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Therapy is treatment that helps someone get better. Some people get better from an illness or injury with treatment, such as exercises or medicine. Other people get help by talking about their worries and feelings with a trained person.
explain: «Therapy means talking with someone trained to help with feelings, such as anger or sadness.» The clues are talking, trained and help. Together they show that therapy is a kind of support, not a punishment.
explain: Therapy is an uncountable noun, so you say some therapy. You can say a therapy when you mean one kind, like speech therapy or physical therapy. To check your meaning, swap in a word like help and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Therapy is treatment to help someone get better from an illness or injury.
fact: Talking therapy means talking with a trained person about worries and feelings, to feel better in your mind.
fact: Speech therapy and physical therapy are two kinds of therapy.
fact: «Therapy dogs visit hospitals, care homes and schools to help people feel calmer.»
fact: Going to therapy shows that someone wants to get better, and asking for help is good and brave.
exercise: «Therapy dogs visit hospitals, care homes and schools to help people feel calmer.» What is the main job of a therapy dog? | To sell food at the hospital | *To help people feel calmer | To guard the school gates | To race other dogs
exercise: Ruby says, «I go to speech therapy because I find it hard to say my r sounds.» What is speech therapy? | A trip to the dentist | A kind of spelling lesson at school | *A treatment that helps someone speak more clearly | A game played with a ball
exercise: Grandma goes to physical therapy after she hurts her knee. What does therapy mean here? | A test at school | *Treatment to help her knee and body get better | A holiday by the sea | A fancy meal out
test: «Therapy means talking with someone trained to help with feelings.» Who gives talking therapy? | A shop assistant | *A trained person | A stranger on the bus | Your pet alone
test: Dev says, «Going to therapy means I want to get better.» What does going to therapy show? | Someone is in trouble with the police | Someone has lost a bet | *Someone wants to get better | Someone is bored
exam: Which best describes therapy? | A type of sport only | A way to make people angry | *Treatment to help someone get better | A kind of weather
